  "worked_solution": "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nLet's compare the coefficients:\n\n- The coefficient of $x$ on the left-hand side is $u,$ and on the right-hand side it is $-1.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nu=-1.\n$$\n\n- The constant term on the left-hand side is $v,$ and on the right-hand side it is $1.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nv=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u+v & =-1+1 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
